`render` replaces main.innerHTML while input event is processing; focusing new input then blur on old input triggers... Actually error "node to be removed is no longer a child" can occur because setting innerHTML causes focus/blur and our focus handler? There's no blur handler. But `main.focus()`? We call render with scroll:false then focus input. Setting innerHTML removes focused input; browser fires blur; maybe no issue. The error is NotFoundError during innerHTML replace, often from the card animation? Hmm.

The issue: in the input handler, render replaces the DOM containing the input while the input event is still dispatching. Then we call input.focus() on the new one. Should be okay but Safari/Chromium can throw if an event handler modifies DOM during blur. We can defer render to next animation frame? But no timers in Code Mode, browser setTimeout is fine. Use requestAnimationFrame or setTimeout(() => render, 0). Then focus new. But re-render per keystroke async; fine. Use a debounce 120ms to avoid too many renders. Simpler: filter cards client-side without full render? Easiest fix: in input handler, call render in `requestAnimationFrame`, then focus via rAF.

```
view.collection.q = ev.target.value;
requestAnimationFrame(() => {
  render({scroll:false});
  const input = $('coll-search');
  if (input) { input.focus({preventScroll:true}); ...}
});
```
But the old input still in DOM until rAF; multiple keystrokes schedule multiple renders. Debounce with a variable and setTimeout 120ms:
```
let searchTimer;
...
clearTimeout(searchTimer);
searchTimer=setTimeout(()=>{ render...; focus...; }, 120);
```
This avoids the exception and is smooth. The value is preserved in view. Add variable.

Also the error might have prevented filter render? Screenshot check. But fix.

Add `let searchTimer = 0;` near top. Clear on navigation? not needed.

Also console error may indicate search input got detached mid-event, but render still likely completed before focus error? It threw at line 478 (main.innerHTML?), no, line 478 is render call line, the stack points to document listener line 478 maybe. It failed at render. So search didn't update. Fix.

